From f00d75611b5118fb567e90e531208ccd4711f0af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:33:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: [TEE Soft Emu-RKP] Add on-device RKP issuance
 and component updates

Add an on-demand native issuer that generates an exportable software
P-256 key, requests certificates through the device's legacy V1 RKP
interface, and assembles an EC-only Keybox.

Expose issuance progress and results in TEE Soft Emu advanced settings.
Reuse the existing Keybox validation and installation path, serialize
issuance with imports and network updates, and recover pending jobs
without automatically issuing another request.

Package the issuer in the independently signed org.system.tee.soft.rkp
APEX with rebootless update support. Add local component installation,
active-version reporting, persistent session recovery and update results.
Restrict installation to the expected package and coordinate updates
with issuance and result handoff.

P.S. Key in native/rkp_issuer/apex/ is testkey, for debug purpose only,
     Please use sign_target_files_apks to sign APEXs with your own key in production build

Co-Authored-by: eltavine <me@eltavine.com>
Change-Id: I9e35625ddf753436b38f463c333dc77f245d23e9
