+# Local RKP component management
+
+## Scope and implementation state (2026-11-14)
+
+The Advanced RKP section now contains the active component version, local APEX
+installation and the last component update result. Only the system user can
+start installation. There is no downloader or update source configuration.
+This patch has received static checks only, not a build or device validation.
+The user reported that the earlier APEX migration builds successfully; that
+does not establish that this new UI/install patch builds or works on-device.
+
+`RkpApexUpdater` owns a single private draft, installation session and result.
+`TeeSoftApplication` initializes persistent exclusion before a fragment can
+start work. A non-exported `RkpApexInstallReceiver` receives the explicit,
+mutable installer PendingIntent and keeps its process alive with goAsync until
+result processing finishes. No private key or RKP material enters this updater.
+
+## Input and install boundary
+
+The document picker accepts any MIME type because APEX types vary between
+providers. The worker copies at most 64 MiB into the application's private
+files directory and synchronizes the file before inspecting it. The URI is not
+retained. A private draft is discarded when confirmation is cancelled, the page
+leaves the foreground, or the process dies; it is never automatically installed.
+
+Checks before confirmation, and again before creating a session:
+
+- The package archive name is exactly `org.system.tee.soft.rkp`, with a version
+  greater than the currently active version.
+- A ZIP entry scan rejects duplicates and more than 1024 entries. The package
+  must have an uncompressed APEX payload image, payload public key and protobuf
+  manifest. Compressed .capex input is not supported.
+- The protobuf manifest is bounded to 64 KiB. Name and version must be present
+  once and must match the container. This is structural validation, not a
+  replacement for platform signature verification.
+- No persisted RKP job is pending and the init helper is stopped. A never-started
+  helper may have no init.svc property: it is accepted only when both state and
+  ro.boottime records are absent and lstat confirms that the control socket does
+  not exist (ENOENT). Other states or inability to inspect are rejected. This
+  relies on the existing app start protocol persisting the job before ctl.start.
+
+The session uses MODE_FULL_INSTALL, INSTALL_APEX, the fixed app package name,
+isStaged=false and USER_ACTION_NOT_REQUIRED. It does not request forced
+non-staged installation, downgrade, signature bypass or allowed-APEX bypass.
+PackageInstaller/apexd verify the actual signed update and activation eligibility.
+Unexpected pending user action is reported and the session is abandoned; this
+updater never forwards an arbitrary installer intent to another activity.
+
+## Permissions and activation query
+
+LineageParts requests INSTALL_PACKAGE_UPDATES, not INSTALL_PACKAGES. Its existing
+system UID satisfies the trusted installer UID check. The permissions XML adds
+the exact allowed-vendor-apex package-to-installer mapping used by
+PackageSessionVerifier for an APEX not listed as a Mainline module. Despite the
+tag name, this check is applied to this custom system APEX too. No global modules
+installer replacement or blanket verification bypass is added.
+
+The originally proposed PackageInfo.isActiveApex query is not used. In this tree,
+that field has a declaration and parcel plumbing but no discovered assignment
+path. The worker reads `/apex/apex-info-list.xml` (bounded to 1 MiB, DTD rejected),
+selects exactly one matching module with isActive=true and caches its version
+for the UI. Missing/duplicate/invalid entries show unavailable. Installation
+completion and every terminal result refresh this authoritative activation list.
+
+SELinux additions are read-only: system_app reads apex_info_file, and exact
+helper status/boot-time properties are mapped to existing readable types.
+The helper's execution domain, HAL grants and socket/control permissions are
+unchanged. No direct apexd Binder access or shell execution is added.
+
+## Exclusion and recovery
+
+Draft preparation and confirmation hold the existing process-wide Keybox job
+lock. Import, URL update and issuance acquisitions also check persistent APEX
+pending state. The component lock covers copy, confirmation, session write,
+commit, system activation and durable result recording. Waiting for user
+confirmation is cancelled on page pause; a submitted session survives it.
+
+Session ID and target version are durably written before session write/commit.
+The startup pending flag blocks all new Keybox work immediately. Recovery only
+queries the recorded session: an unsealed/uncommitted draft is abandoned, while
+a sealed or committed session stays pending and is polled. The same installer's
+unsealed drafts for this exact package are also cleaned on startup to cover the
+createSession-before-persist crash window. Neither recovery nor an uncertain
+commit reply resubmits an installation or requests another issuance.
+
+If a session disappears without its result broadcast, an exact matching active
+version confirms activation. Otherwise the outcome is shown as unconfirmed,
+with the current active version displayed separately. Normal failure broadcasts
+preserve the platform status and bounded diagnostic message. Draft/provider
+errors use local messages rather than persisting a URI-bearing exception.
+If result-state persistence fails, operations remain excluded in this process;
+restart the application to reconcile durable state. An unresolved sealed or
+committed system session remains excluded, without an arbitrary timeout unlock.
+
+This is application coordination, not a system-wide installation lock. An
+external ADB/root/system installer can bypass it and terminate a busy helper.
+All apps sharing UID 1000 remain inside the pre-existing trust boundary.
+There is no automatic rollback following a server-side issuance failure.
+
+## Verification ledger
+
+Passed static checks: Java tree-sitter parsing, XML parsing, all new string
+references and three-locale placeholder parity, manifest-to-class wiring,
+fixed package/session/result wiring, and whitespace/diff checks. Reviewed the
+current PackageInstaller permission and consistency checks, SystemConfig
+allowed-vendor-apex parsing, ApexInfoList schema, protobuf field definitions,
+init service state transitions and SELinux read grants.
+
+No Java compilation, policy compilation, executable tests, device operation or
+Git commit was performed. A future authorized build/device validation must cover:
+
+- Both fresh-boot and previously used helper idle detection; active-version
+  display and all new read permissions under enforcing SELinux.
+- A higher-version update signed with the ROM's two signing identities, no
+  reboot, and the next issuer process using the newly activated mount.
+- Wrong package, inconsistent manifests, invalid signatures, same/lower version,
+  oversized input and malformed package rejected with the old active version
+  still correctly reported.
+- Confirmation cancellation, rotation/backgrounding, process death before/after
+  commit, lost result broadcast and duplicate callback handling.
+- Import, download and signing exclusion through result ACK/helper exit; no
+  automatic installation or issuance retry after interruption.
